&lt;p&gt;WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&amp;nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&amp;nbsp;in a single company –&amp;nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&amp;nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://wpp.com/&quot; data-outlook-id=&quot;2714312b-312f-4651-9f88-d8a4e47547bc&quot;&gt;WPP.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-olk-copy-source=&quot;MessageBody&quot;&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Senior Medical Writer (SMW) to join our rapidly growing content development team, providing leading edge Medical Communications services to global pharmaceutical companies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will drive ideation and development of a wide range of scientific/medical education assets and activities, including presentations (for internal trainings, external standalone events, and congress symposia), digital assets (delivered online or at live events), and audiovisual pieces (e.g. interviews, animations).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who fully understands, and who has mastered, the SMW role. Typically this would entail at least four years’ experience at an agency with MedComms focus.&amp;nbsp; Excellent PowerPoint skills are mandatory. &amp;nbsp;Recent experience around immunotherapy and immunosuppression would be highly desirable. The position will include regular, direct contact with the client team and with expert physicians involved in asset development. Occasional travel will be required&lt;/p&gt;
